- The value can't contain `]]>`, which would end the section. The check happens when the node is written, and it throws an `XmlException` ("CDATA must not contain ']]>'."). The node doesn't split the value into two sections for you.
- A CDATA section in parsed XML stays a CDATA section in the tree and is written back as one.
- A `null` value is stored as an empty string.
